%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4b3f2a8c8f344355b16a4d4296ae3f98, type: 3}
  m_Name: Scarab
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  vesselClass: 12
  entries:
  - Element: 1
    AbilityLabel: Cavitation Blast
    AbilityDescription: 'The mantis-shrimp punch that rides the dash: push the RIGHT
      THUMBSTICK to the perimeter and the dash throws a swept PLATE - a broad disc
      lying flat across your course, starting on the hull and sweeping along the
      dash - shredding prisms, killing fauna (a creature dies when its body prisms
      are destroyed) and elementally debuffing any opposing pilot it engulfs.
      Everything it claims is thrown the way the punch travelled, not away from a
      point. Charge shortens its cooldown - authored on ScarabCavitationBlast,
      x1 at rest -> x0.5 at level 10, so the generic map multiplier stays 1.0 (no
      double-dip). THE DASH ITSELF IS FREE AND NEVER PACED: only the punch waits,
      so a recharging blast never costs you the dodge. No input-event binding: the
      juke polls the right thumbstick directly (ScarabJukeController), and the enum
      has no member for it - InputEvents.RightStickAction (1) and
      OnlyRightStickAction (11) are both raised from the right TRIGGER despite
      their names, and 11 is what this entry used to claim, which would have taught
      the four-icon row that the blast is a trigger ability.'
    Input: 0
    MultiplierAtFullLevel: 1
    MinMultiplier: 1
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Cavitation Shear
    UpgradeDescription: The blast destroys SHIELDED prisms outright instead of only
      shedding their shields (per-use snapshot at fire time, via the explosion's
      devastating flag). Super-shielded mass is still untouchable - that tier has
      no sanctioned breaker.
  - Element: 2
    AbilityLabel: Switch
    AbilityDescription: Mass grows the switch structure - ring aperture and the span
      of the prism fill across its mouth (authored on
      PlaceSwitchActionSO.switchScale ElementalFloat, x1 -> x2.5 at level 10; the
      generic map multiplier stays 1.0 to avoid double-dipping).
    Input: 6
    MultiplierAtFullLevel: 1
    MinMultiplier: 1
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Armored Switch
    UpgradeDescription: The switch is built from SHIELDED prisms (the sanctioned
      shield tier - never SuperShield), snapshotted at placement so a switch keeps
      the armour it was born with. An opposing ball now caroms off it and sheds one
      shield per prism instead of eating straight through, which is what turns a
      switch placed in front of someone else's shot into real defence.
  - Element: 3
    AbilityLabel: Ball Forge
    AbilityDescription: 'Space scales the ball you mint: x1 at rest, x4 at level 10.
      Unlike the other three rows the map''s generic multiplier IS the carrier here
      (MultiplierAtFullLevel 4), read live at forge time and stamped once - a ball
      keeps the size it was born with. No input binding: you forge by flying THROUGH
      an omni crystal at the speed and heading you want the ball to leave with, so
      making a ball is a piece of driving. The launch velocity is the vessel''s TRUE
      motion including the dash channel, so dashing into a crystal and dashing into
      a resting ball produce the same trajectory.'
    Input: 0
    MultiplierAtFullLevel: 4
    MinMultiplier: 0.5
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel:
    UpgradeDescription: '(open design slot) Space 5 is deliberately unfilled - the
      design notes assign Space the ball''s size and name no qualitative upgrade for
      it. Do not invent one without sign-off (SCARAB.md section 7).'
  - Element: 4
    AbilityLabel: Throttle
    AbilityDescription: Time raises the top speed of the throttle ramp (authored on
      the transformer's ThrottleScalerMultiplier ElementalFloat, x1 -> x1.5 at level
      10; the generic map Time multiplier stays 1.0 - the no-double-dip pin). The
      throttle is analog on the right trigger, thrust always along the nose, and
      releasing it is the only brake.
    Input: 1
    MultiplierAtFullLevel: 1
    MinMultiplier: 1
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Snap Dash
    UpgradeDescription: 'Double-tap the THROTTLE (right trigger) for a short forward
      burst - a gap-closer along the nose. Distinct from the right-stick dash, which
      is base kit and always available: Snap Dash is the throttle''s upgrade, not the
      dash''s.'
